{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791228878,"nonce":"L25I2oAX7zD2/R8m2GGO5yR86lI=","message":"Under the serve design (1cd4233e5f42962121a0103f55d874415a920cfb) back-to-back empty polls still average about 4 ms. Logging shows they alternate: one poll's serve event is handled within 0.3 ms; the next one's isn't dequeued at all, and that run ends at the display frame (about 7 ms). The following poll then sees both serve events. So after a run whose monitor ran its nested fetch, the next event posted before -[NSApplication run] goes unseen until the frame.\n\nTried, no change: ending the monitor's loop on a posted sentinel it fetches back (so the last fetch returns an event); returning the serve event instead of nil after -stop:; posting the serve event atStart:YES.","files":null}]}